{
  "summary": "Calls DisableNextWrite() at the start of each fuzz iteration across mempool and package evaluation fuzz targets (tx_pool, tx_pool_standard, tx_package_eval, ephemeral_package_eval, and validation_load_mempool). This prevents periodic chainstate flush-to-disk logic from executing unpredictably across inputs.",
  "problem": "Mempool acceptance calls FlushStateToDisk(PERIODIC), which checks a static m_next_write timer in chainstate. Because the timer carries over between fuzz iterations, an input's execution path depends on whichever inputs ran before it, causing non-deterministic coverage tracking and preventing crash inputs from reproducing in isolation.",
  "evidence": [
    "Author measured periodic-write branch hits across shuffled replays on qa-assets using contrib/devtools/deterministic-fuzz-coverage, showing branch hits dropping from variable rates (e.g. 4 vs 17 in tx_pool) down to 0 in all five targets (PR description).",
    "Fix follows the approach merged for process_message(s) and cmpctblock in PR #32822 (PR description)."
  ],
